<title>NETHERLANDS: Pakhoed takes stake in British agencies.</title>
<headline>Pakhoed takes stake in British agencies.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch tank storage and shipping group Pakhoed NV said on Friday it had taken a 50 percent stake in the Genchem agency companies in Ipswich, Avonmouth and Liverpool.</p>
<p>It said Pakhoed Agenturen B.V. Rotterdam and Genchem London already operated tanker agencies under the name Clarkson Brothers and Casper Ltd in Middlesborough, Hull and Immingham.</p>
<p>The new company would operate under the name Clarkson Shipping Ltd.</p>
<p>The terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
